cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use NoiseBridge in your research, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "NoiseBridge: Zero-Overhead Syndrome Decoding via Centering-Matrix SNN"
version: 0.3.0
date-released: "2026-05-13"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/MousMou/noisebridge"
url: "https://github.com/MousMou/noisebridge"
authors:
  - name: "FractKit Project"
    email: partrabajo613@gmail.com
abstract: >
  NoiseBridge applies a centering-matrix Syndrome Error Corrector (SNN-SEC)
  as post-processing for quantum measurement distributions. Zero additional
  QPU shots required. Achieves LER_SNN = LER_raw (zero decoder overhead) on
  IBM Kingston real hardware at p=0.25, and 1.72x improvement over the standard
  lookup decoder at p=0.10 (Surface Code d=3, depth=26, CZ=25, SWAP=0).
  Combined REM + SNN pipeline validated on IQM Garnet real QPU: avg +0.057
  fidelity (6/6 circuits positive).
keywords:
  - quantum computing
  - quantum error correction
  - noise mitigation
  - spiking neural network
  - surface code
  - syndrome decoding
  - NISQ
  - IBM Quantum
  - IQM
references:
